IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sea-schooling`

-- School Education Act 1999 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the parent of a child of school age, or the adult responsible for the child (s 11A(1)(c)) -- the baseline's seat,
--     whose 47 questions are asked here by calling the baseline's functions in sea-schooling.l4;
--   * the child or student -- bound by s 23 (attendance) and s 38(2) ($10), by s 36(3) when stopped by an attendance
--     officer ($200), protected by ss 41-42 before a prosecution, and, as an adult student or a student who has turned 18,
--     meeting the fees sections in person (ss 97, 98, 105, 106(1)(b));
--   * a person who employs a child, or would like to -- bound by s 29 ($5 000).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The principal, the
-- chief executive officer, the Minister, an attendance officer and an Attendance Panel are never seats: what they may or
-- must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. They are:
--   * for the parent: `my child has been away from school` (the excused-absence, s 23, s 38(1) and s 38-prosecution
--     questions, which the Act ties to a day of non-attendance); `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an
--     Attendance Panel` (ss 26, 39, 40); `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment`
--     (ss 11A-11H); `my child works, or would work, for someone` (s 29); and `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a
--     government school` (ss 75-79 and 97-106, which Part 3 confines to government schools);
--   * for the student: `I have been away from school`; `I am leaving, or have left, school for a course, training or
--     employment`; `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`;
--   * the employer has none: every employer question arises for every employer.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (the periods of ss 5 and 6, who is a parent, the duty to enrol,
-- the penalties) takes no situation input. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, so no situation helper reads an
-- enumeration through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's records (`My child's arrangements`, `My child's
-- absence`, `My child's residence`, `The school's offer`) are taken as the baseline takes them.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `School Education Act 1999 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child`
    `I am the child or student`
    `I employ a child, or would like to`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Year answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    year HAS `which year` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Day answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it ends on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Priority group` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `priority group` HAS `group number` IS A NUMBER

-- The baseline's `Limit` (s 98(3), reg 61), with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Charge limit` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no more than` HAS dollars IS A NUMBER
    `none may be charged or sought`
    `no limit is set by regulation 61`

-- The baseline's `What I must do` (ss 11D, 11G, 11H), with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Steps for the option` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `give the Minister notice under s 11D as soon as practicable after the arrangements are made`
    `apply for the Minister's approval under s 11G, then give notice under s 11H as soon as practicable after the employment starts`
    `nothing will make it count: the option is not one s 11B(1) allows`

-- The student's two offences (ss 36(3), 38(2)).
DECLARE `Student offence` IS ONE OF
    `not attending school as section 23 requires`
    `not telling an attendance officer my name, address, age or school, or telling it falsely`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the new seats need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`as an amount` `the number` MEANS amount `the number`

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Year answer`
`as a year` `the number` MEANS year `the number`

GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`as a day` `the date` MEANS `it ends on` `the date`

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Priority group`
`as a priority group` `the number` MEANS `priority group` `the number`

GIVEN `the limit` IS A Limit
GIVETH A `Charge limit`
`as a charge limit` `the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `at most` d THEN `no more than` d
    WHEN `none may be imposed or sought` THEN `none may be charged or sought`
    WHEN `no limit is prescribed by regulation 61` THEN `no limit is set by regulation 61`

GIVEN `the steps` IS A `What I must do`
GIVETH A `Steps for the option`
`as steps` `the steps` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the steps`
    WHEN `give notice to the Minister under section 11D as soon as practicable after the arrangements are made` THEN `give the Minister notice under s 11D as soon as practicable after the arrangements are made`
    WHEN `apply for the Minister's approval under section 11G, then give notice under section 11H as soon as practicable after the employment starts` THEN `apply for the Minister's approval under s 11G, then give notice under s 11H as soon as practicable after the employment starts`
    WHEN `nothing will make it count: the option is not one section 11B(1) allows` THEN `nothing will make it count: the option is not one s 11B(1) allows`

-- The student's offence as the baseline's penalty table names it. Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Student offence`
GIVETH AN Offence
`the baseline's offence for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not attending school as section 23 requires` THEN `my child not attending`
    WHEN `not telling an attendance officer my name, address, age or school, or telling it falsely` THEN `my child not telling an attendance officer name, address, age or school`

-- s 106(1): a fee or charge "may be recovered as a debt ... (b) in the case of a student who has turned 18 or who is a
-- prescribed child, from the student". (2): before any action the chief executive officer is to ensure the inquiries,
-- the reasonably practicable steps and the regard to the person's circumstances and capacity to pay (read as conditions,
-- as the baseline reads s 106(2) for the parent). Who is a "prescribed child" is for the regulations: a fact.
GIVEN `turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prescribed child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `inquiries made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `steps taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `circumstances considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(1)(b), (2) -- the fee or charge may be recovered from the student` IF
        (`turned 18` OR `a prescribed child`)
    AND `inquiries made`
    AND `steps taken`
    AND `circumstances considered`

-- s 29(1): "A person must not employ or permit to be employed a child of compulsory school age during the hours when the
-- child is required to" attend or take part; (2) unpaid work for the purpose of gain is employment; (3) the exceptions.
-- The baseline's `May my child work during school hours` is s 29(1) and (3) from the parent's seat; the employer
-- commits the offence where the child works for the employer for gain and that answer is no. A child who does not work
-- for gain is not "employed" (s 29(2) extends the word to unpaid work for gain, and nothing extends it further): a fork
-- recorded in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `works for gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `required hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 24 arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved under s 11G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(1) -- the employer commits the offence` IF
        `works for gain`
    AND (NOT (`May my child work during school hours` `compulsory school age` `required hours` `a s 24 arrangement` `in the programme` `approved under s 11G`))

§§ `For the parent of a child of school age (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (sea-schooling.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 4, 5, 6 -- kindergarten, the compulsory education period and the final two years`

@export In which year does my child's precompulsory (kindergarten) period begin (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
GIVETH A `Year answer`
`In which year does my child's kindergarten period begin` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `as a year` (`the first year of my child's precompulsory education period` `my child's date of birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export In which year does my child's precompulsory (kindergarten) period end (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
GIVETH A `Year answer`
`In which year does my child's kindergarten period end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `as a year` (`the last year of my child's precompulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my child in the precompulsory (kindergarten) period on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child in the kindergarten period on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in the precompulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export In which year does my child's compulsory education period begin (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
GIVETH A `Year answer`
`In which year does my child's compulsory education period begin` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `as a year` (`the first year of my child's compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On what day does my child's compulsory education period end (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`On what day does my child's compulsory education period end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `as a day` (`the last day of my child's compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my child in the compulsory education period on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
      `graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child in the compulsory education period on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in the compulsory education period` `my child's date of birth` `on` `graduated`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my child in the final two years of compulsory education (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child in the final two years of compulsory education` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in the final years of compulsory education` `my child's date of birth` `on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4, 11A -- am I a parent`

@export Am I a parent of my child for the School Education Act 1999 (WA) (s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's long-term care, welfare and development
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a parent of my child under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a parent under this Act` `long-term responsibility` `day-to-day responsibility`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I a parent who must ensure my child is enrolled and attends (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 9(2), 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's long-term care, welfare and development
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a parent who answers for enrolment and attendance` `long-term responsibility` `day-to-day responsibility`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I give the notices for my child's final-years options as a parent (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 11A(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is taking up, or has taken up, a course, an apprenticeship, employment or another option instead of school in the final two years of compulsory education (ss 11A-11H)
      `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's long-term care, welfare and development
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
      `the Minister's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is of the opinion that no such parent is reasonably available
      `an adult responsible for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an adult who is responsible for the child
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I give the notices for my child's final-years options` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`Am I a parent for the final-years options` `long-term responsibility` `day-to-day responsibility` `the Minister's opinion` `an adult responsible for the child`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 9, 10, 11 -- the duty to enrol`

@export Must my child be enrolled on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 9(1), 11(2), 11F(2), 11H(5)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
      `graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
      `the arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements` @desc Your child's schooling, home education, exemption or final-years arrangements
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my child be enrolled on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Must my child be enrolled` `my child's date of birth` `on` `graduated` `the arrangements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do my child's arrangements satisfy the duty to enrol (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 10(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements` @desc Your child's schooling, home education, exemption or final-years arrangements
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do my child's arrangements satisfy the duty to enrol` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Do the arrangements satisfy the duty to enrol` `the arrangements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in breach of the duty to have my child enrolled (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 9(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
      `graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
      `the arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements` @desc Your child's schooling, home education, exemption or final-years arrangements
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in breach of the duty to have my child enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`Am I in breach of section 9(2)` `my child's date of birth` `on` `graduated` `the arrangements` `day-to-day responsibility`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I be prosecuted for not having my child enrolled (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 9(3), 41(1a), 42(1a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the CEO's certificate under section 9(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief executive officer has certified that reasonably practicable steps were taken to secure enrolment
      `a notified option my child is not following` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is under a s 11D or 11H notice and is not participating as s 11I requires
      `the option is an apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the option your child is not following is an apprenticeship
      `a certificate under section 42(1a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a certificate has been given that steps were taken to secure participation and non-participation continued
      `a Panel advised or offered assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Attendance Panel has given advice or offered assistance (s 40(2)(b))
      `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to follow that advice or accept that assistance
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be prosecuted for not having my child enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `yes if` (`May I be prosecuted under section 9(2)` `the CEO's certificate under section 9(3)` `a notified option my child is not following` `the option is an apprenticeship` `a certificate under section 42(1a)` `a Panel advised or offered assistance` `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 11B-11H -- leaving school in the final two years`

@export Is my child's participation full-time (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 11C; regs 11B, 11C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is taking up, or has taken up, a course, an apprenticeship, employment or another option instead of school in the final two years of compulsory education (ss 11A-11H)
      `the total participation value` IS A NUMBER @desc The total participation value of your child's options, in per cent (a single full-time option counts 100)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child's participation in the options full-time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child's participation full-time` `the total participation value`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my child take this option instead of school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 11B, 11C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is taking up, or has taken up, a course, an apprenticeship, employment or another option instead of school in the final two years of compulsory education (ss 11A-11H)
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
      `the option` IS AN Option @desc The course, training or employment your child would take up
      `the total participation value` IS A NUMBER @desc The total participation value of your child's options, in per cent (a single full-time option counts 100)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my child take this option instead of school in the final two years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my child take this option instead of school` `my child's date of birth` `on` `the option` `the total participation value`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What must I do so that my child's option counts instead of school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 11D, 11G, 11H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is taking up, or has taken up, a course, an apprenticeship, employment or another option instead of school in the final two years of compulsory education (ss 11A-11H)
      `the option` IS AN Option @desc The course, training or employment your child would take up
GIVETH A `Steps for the option`
`What must I do so that my child's option counts instead of school` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment`
        THEN `as steps` (`What must I do for the option to count` `the option`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my section 11D notice in force (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 11D(7), 11E, 11F(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is taking up, or has taken up, a course, an apprenticeship, employment or another option instead of school in the final two years of compulsory education (ss 11A-11H)
      `I gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Minister notice of the arrangements
      `a combination of courses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arrangements are a combination of courses
      `the Minister acknowledged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has given you a formal written acknowledgment of the choice of courses
      `my child still participates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is still participating in every notified option
      `I cancelled it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have cancelled the notice
      `the compulsory period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child's compulsory education period has ended
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my notice of my child's option in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child is leaving, or has left, school for a course, training or employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my section 11D notice in force` `I gave the notice` `a combination of courses` `the Minister acknowledged it` `my child still participates` `I cancelled it` `the compulsory period has ended`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 29 -- work in school hours`

@export May my child work (or may I let my child work) during school hours (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 29)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child works, or would work, for someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child works, or would work, for someone, paid or unpaid for the purpose of gain (s 29(2))
      `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age (for s 29, this includes a child under a s 11D or 11H notice, s 29(1a))
      `during required hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is during hours when your child is required to attend school or take part in its programme
      `a section 24 arrangement authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written s 24 arrangement with the principal authorises the work
      `part of the programme, within its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is part of your child's educational programme and consistent with its terms
      `approved under section 11G, within its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved the employment under s 11G and it is consistent with that approval
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my child work, or may I let my child work, during school hours` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child works, or would work, for someone`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my child work during school hours` `of compulsory school age` `during required hours` `a section 24 arrangement authorises it` `part of the programme, within its terms` `approved under section 11G, within its terms`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23, 25, 27, 30, 38 -- attendance, excused absence and the offences`

@export Is my child excused from school that day (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 25, 27, 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child has been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution for absences arise only then)
      `the absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day your child was away and what you told the school
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child excused from school on that day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child has been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child excused that day` `the absence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my child in breach of the attendance requirement that day (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child has been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution for absences arise only then)
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
      `enrolled at a school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is enrolled at a school
      `the absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day your child was away and what you told the school
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child in breach of the attendance requirement on that day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child has been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in breach of section 23` `my child's date of birth` `on` `enrolled at a school` `the absence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in breach of my duty to ensure my child attends (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child has been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution for absences arise only then)
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day your child was away)
      `the absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day your child was away and what you told the school
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have legal responsibility for your child's day-to-day care, welfare and development
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in breach of my duty to ensure my child attends school` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child has been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Am I in breach of section 38(1)` `my child's date of birth` `on` `the absence` `day-to-day responsibility`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I (or my child) can be fined for this offence (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 9(2), 11AA(2), 13(3), 27(4), 29(1), 36(3), 37, 38, 43(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I, or my child, can be fined for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN `as an amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I be prosecuted for my child's absences (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 41(1), 42(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child has been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child has missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution for absences arise only then)
      `a certificate under section 42(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Panel or the chief executive officer has certified that reasonably practicable steps were taken and the breaches continued
      `a Panel advised or offered assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Attendance Panel has given advice or offered assistance (s 40(2)(b))
      `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to follow that advice or accept that assistance
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be prosecuted for my child's absences` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child has been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I be prosecuted under section 38` `a certificate under section 42(1)` `a Panel advised or offered assistance` `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 26, 39, 40 -- Attendance Panels`

@export May my child's case be referred to an Attendance Panel by this person (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 26, 40)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child's attendance, or participation in a notified course or employment, has been or may be referred to an Attendance Panel (ss 26, 39, 40)
      `the referrer` IS A Referrer @desc Who wants to refer the case
      `the ground` IS A Ground @desc Why
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my child's case be referred to an Attendance Panel by this person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my child's case be referred to an Attendance Panel` `the referrer` `the ground`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the Attendance Panel do this (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 40)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child's attendance, or participation in a notified course or employment, has been or may be referred to an Attendance Panel (ss 26, 39, 40)
      `the step` IS A PanelStep @desc What the Panel might do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Attendance Panel do this` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the Panel do this` `the step`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May this Attendance Panel deal with my child's case (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 39)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child's attendance, or participation in a notified course or employment, has been or may be referred to an Attendance Panel (ss 26, 39, 40)
      `members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are on the Panel
      `parent or community representatives` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are parent or community representatives
      `the chair is a department employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chairperson is employed in the education department
      `a member teaches at my child's school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member is on the teaching staff (or is the principal) of your child's school
      `a member has a child at my child's school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member is a parent of a child enrolled at your child's school
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this Attendance Panel deal with my child's case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel`
        THEN `yes if` (`May this Panel deal with my child's case` `members` `parent or community representatives` `the chair is a department employee` `a member teaches at my child's school` `a member has a child at my child's school`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May someone represent us before the Attendance Panel (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 39(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child's attendance, or participation in a notified course or employment, has been or may be referred to an Attendance Panel (ss 26, 39, 40)
      `the Panel has determined representation is needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Panel has decided the process will not work effectively without representation
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May someone represent us before the Attendance Panel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child's case has been, or may be, referred to an Attendance Panel`
        THEN `yes if` (`May someone represent us before the Panel` `the Panel has determined representation is needed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 75-79 -- which government school must take my child`

@export Is my child qualified by residence to enrol at a government school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 76; regs 12-14A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child qualified by residence to enrol at a government school` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child qualified by residence` `the residence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my child entitled to enrol at this local-intake school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 76, 78)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
      `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age (for s 29, this includes a child under a s 11D or 11H notice, s 29(1a))
      `the school` IS A `The school's offer` @desc Whether you live in the school's intake area, and what it has available
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my child entitled to enrol at this local-intake school` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child entitled to enrol at the local-intake school` `the residence` `of compulsory school age` `the school`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

