        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the principal of our local-intake school enrol my child (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 75)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `the residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where your child lives and their residence or visa status
      `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is of compulsory school age (for s 29, this includes a child under a s 11D or 11H notice, s 29(1a))
      `the school` IS A `The school's offer` @desc Whether you live in the school's intake area, and what it has available
      `I applied in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a completed application in the form the chief executive officer approved
      `already enrolled elsewhere, for under 4 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is already enrolled at a school and the stay applied for is likely to be under 4 weeks
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the principal of our local-intake school enrol my child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must the principal enrol my child` `the residence` `of compulsory school age` `the school` `I applied in the approved form` `already enrolled elsewhere, for under 4 weeks`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export From outside the intake area, in which priority group is my child (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 16)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `qualifies for a specialist programme there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child qualifies for a specialist programme at that school this year
      `a sibling enrolled there, other than in a specialist programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a brother or sister is enrolled there this year, other than to take part in a specialist programme
GIVETH A `Priority group`
`From outside the intake area, in which priority group is my child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `as a priority group` (`my child's priority group from outside the intake area` `qualifies for a specialist programme there` `a sibling enrolled there, other than in a specialist programme`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For a kindergarten place at a local-intake school, in which priority group is my child (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 15(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `we live in its intake area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in the school's intake area
      `a sibling enrolled there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a brother or sister is enrolled there that year
GIVETH A `Priority group`
`For a kindergarten place, in which priority group is my child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `as a priority group` (`my child's priority group for kindergarten` `we live in its intake area` `a sibling enrolled there`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

