@export Can unpaid school charges be recovered from me as a debt (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `my child is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child is under 18
      `the reasons were inquired into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether inquiries were made into why the charge was not paid
      `every practicable step was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all reasonably practicable steps were taken to recover it
      `my circumstances were considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your circumstances and capacity to pay were taken into account
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can unpaid school charges be recovered from me as a debt` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the charges be recovered from me` `my child is under 18` `the reasons were inquired into` `every practicable step was taken` `my circumstances were considered`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a government school can charge in fees for instruction in a year (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 63(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most a government school can charge in fees for instruction in a year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `as an amount` (`the most a fee for instruction can be`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As an adult student, is my child exempt from fees for instruction (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 64)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child attends, or is to be enrolled at, a government school (the enrolment rules of ss 75-79 and the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `my child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your child's date of birth
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year
      `a curriculum-based programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programme is based on the learning outcomes in the outline of curriculum and assessment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As an adult student, is my child exempt from fees for instruction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child` THEN
        IF `my child goes to, or is to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my adult child exempt from fees for instruction` `my child's date of birth` `the year` `a curriculum-based programme`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the child or student (ss 6, 23, 25, 38(2), 36(3), 41, 42, 97-106)`

-- s 23 binds the student; s 38(2) makes a child of compulsory school age enrolled at a school who does not comply
-- liable to a fine of $10; s 36(3) to $200; ss 41 and 42 bar a prosecution under s 38, which includes s 38(2). An adult
-- student, and a student who has turned 18, meets the fees sections in person (ss 97, 98, 105, 106(1)(b)).

§§§ `ss 6, 11B -- my compulsory education period, and leaving in the final two years`

@export On what day does my compulsory education period end (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day you were away)
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`On what day does my compulsory education period end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN `as a day` (`the last day of my child's compulsory education period` `my date of birth` `the date`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in my compulsory education period, and so of compulsory school age, on this date (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day you were away)
      `I have graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that date
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I of compulsory school age on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in the compulsory education period` `my date of birth` `the date` `I have graduated`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in the final two years of compulsory education (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day you were away)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in the final two years of compulsory education` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in the final years of compulsory education` `my date of birth` `the date`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I take this course, training or employment instead of school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 11B, 11C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am leaving, or have left, school for a course, training or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking up, or have taken up, a course, an apprenticeship, employment or another option instead of school in the final two years of compulsory education (s 11B)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day you were away)
      `my option` IS AN Option @desc The course, training or employment you would take up
      `the total participation value of my options` IS A NUMBER @desc The total participation value of your options, in per cent (a single full-time option counts 100)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I take this option instead of school` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I am leaving, or have left, school for a course, training or employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my child take this option instead of school` `my date of birth` `the date` `my option` `the total participation value of my options`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23, 25, 36, 38, 41, 42 -- attendance, and the offences`

@export Am I in breach of the attendance requirement that day (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution arise only then)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date your question is about (for an absence, the day you were away)
      `I am enrolled at a school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled at a school
      `my absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day you were away, and what you or your parent told the school
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in breach of the attendance requirement on that day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I have been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in breach of section 23` `my date of birth` `the date` `I am enrolled at a school` `my absence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I excused from school that day (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 25, 27, 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution arise only then)
      `my absence` IS A `My child's absence` @desc The day you were away, and what you or your parent told the school
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my absence excused on that day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I have been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child excused that day` `my absence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I be prosecuted for not attending school (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 38(2), 41(1), 42(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been away from school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have missed school on one or more days (the questions on excused absence, the attendance requirement and prosecution arise only then)
      `a certificate under section 42(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Panel or the chief executive officer has certified that reasonably practicable steps were taken and the breaches continued
      `a Panel advised or offered assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Attendance Panel has given advice or offered assistance (s 40(2)(b))
      `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to follow that advice or accept that assistance
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be prosecuted for not attending school` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I have been away from school`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I be prosecuted under section 38` `a certificate under section 42(1)` `a Panel advised or offered assistance` `I did not follow the advice or accept the assistance`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not attending school, or for not telling an attendance officer who I am (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 36(3), 38(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my offence` IS A `Student offence` @desc The offence: not attending school as s 23 requires (s 38(2)); or, when stopped by an attendance officer, not giving your name, address, age or school, or giving false or misleading information (s 36(3))
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for this offence as a student` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN `as an amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for` (`the baseline's offence for` `my offence`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 97-106, regs 62-64 -- fees and charges at a government school`

@export Am I an adult student this year (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 97)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend, or are to be enrolled at, a government school (the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the school year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an adult student this year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child an adult student` `my date of birth` `the school year`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I an overseas student (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 97; reg 62)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend, or are to be enrolled at, a government school (the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `my residence` IS A `My child's residence` @desc Where you live, and your residence or visa status
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an overseas student` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my child an overseas student` `my residence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the government school charge a fee for my instruction (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 98(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend, or are to be enrolled at, a government school (the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `the component` IS A Component @desc What the instruction is for
      `I am an overseas student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an overseas student
      `I am an adult student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an adult student
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the government school charge me a fee for instruction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the school charge a fee for instruction` `the component` `I am an overseas student` `I am an adult student`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As an adult student, am I exempt from fees for instruction (School Education Regulations 2000 (WA) reg 64)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend, or are to be enrolled at, a government school (the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the school year` IS A NUMBER @desc The school year
      `my programme is curriculum-based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your programme is based on the learning outcomes in the outline of curriculum and assessment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As an adult student, am I exempt from fees for instruction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my adult child exempt from fees for instruction` `my date of birth` `the school year` `my programme is curriculum-based`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be kept out of classes because the charges have not been paid (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 105)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend, or are to be enrolled at, a government school (the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `I am an overseas student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an overseas student
      `I am an adult student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an adult student
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be kept out of classes because the charges are unpaid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my child be excluded for unpaid charges` `I am an overseas student` `I am an adult student`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can unpaid school fees or charges be recovered from me, the student, as a debt (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 106(1)(b), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend, or are to be enrolled at, a government school (the fees and charges of ss 97-106 are for government schools only)
      `I have turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have turned 18
      `I am a prescribed child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a child of a class prescribed by the regulations for the purpose ("prescribed child")
      `the reasons were inquired into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether inquiries were made into why the charge was not paid
      `every practicable step was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all reasonably practicable steps were taken to recover it
      `my circumstances were considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your circumstances and capacity to pay were taken into account
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can unpaid school charges be recovered from me as a student` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the child or student` THEN
        IF `I go to, or am to enrol at, a government school`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 106(1)(b), (2) -- the fee or charge may be recovered from the student` `I have turned 18` `I am a prescribed child` `the reasons were inquired into` `every practicable step was taken` `my circumstances were considered`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person who employs a child, or would like to (ss 6, 29)`

-- s 29(1): "A person must not employ or permit to be employed a child of compulsory school age during the hours when
-- the child is required to" attend school or take part in its programme. Every question here arises for every
-- employer, so none takes a situation input (D8).

§§§ `s 29 -- employing a child during school hours`

@export Is this child of compulsory school age on the day of the work (School Education Act 1999 (WA) ss 4, 6, 29(1a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's date of birth
      `the day of the work` IS A DATE @desc The day the child works, or would work, for you
      `the child has graduated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child had met the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school by that day
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this child of compulsory school age on the day of the work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ a child, or would like to` THEN `yes if` (`Is my child in the compulsory education period` `the child's date of birth` `the day of the work` `the child has graduated`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me to employ this child, or let the child be employed, at this time (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 29(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the child works for me for gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child works, or would work, for you or with your permission for the purpose of gain, whether or not the child is paid (s 29(2))
      `the child is of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is of compulsory school age, including a child under a s 11D or 11H notice (s 29(1a))
      `during the child's required hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is during hours when the child is required to attend school or take part in its educational programme
      `a section 24 arrangement authorises the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written arrangement with the principal under s 24 authorises the work
      `the work is part of the child's educational programme, within its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is included in the child's educational programme and is consistent with its terms and conditions
      `the Minister approved the employment under section 11G, within its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved the employment under s 11G and it is consistent with the approval's terms and conditions
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to employ this child at this time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ a child, or would like to` THEN `yes if` (`s 29(1) -- the employer commits the offence` `the child works for me for gain` `the child is of compulsory school age` `during the child's required hours` `a section 24 arrangement authorises the work` `the work is part of the child's educational programme, within its terms` `the Minister approved the employment under section 11G, within its terms`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for employing a child, or letting a child be employed, during school hours (School Education Act 1999 (WA) s 29(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for employing a child during school hours` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ a child, or would like to` THEN `as an amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for` `employing my child, or letting my child be employed, in school hours`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
